Decision: reject before distributed timing.  The candidate loses every core
and total point.  At M32 both GEMMs regress about 3%, so the result is not an
isolated epilogue or route effect.  The extra cp.async group, wait, and
schedule perturbation cost more than any activation latency hidden underneath
the current two-stage packed-weight pipeline.
